1. Container image (Dockerfile, built in your AWS account by AWS CodeBuild)

Base image: python:3.12.16-slim from public.ecr.aws/docker/library/python, pinned by digest. Python is under the
PSF License Agreement (https://docs.python.org/3/license.html) and pip (which the Dockerfile upgrades to 26.2.2,
uses to install the packages, then removes) under the MIT License; the Debian packages in the image, including the
security updates the build installs, are under their own licenses (https://www.debian.org/legal/licenses/).

Python packages that the Dockerfile installs for the CPU image: torch 2.14.1 (CPU build), strands-decider 0.3.0,
transformers 5.20.2, strands-agents 1.62.0, mcp 1.30.0 and boto3, with the dependencies they resolved to on
11 November 2026 (Python 3.12). Dependency versions can differ when you build. To list them for your own image,
run pip-licenses --with-urls inside it.

