1a. Optional GPU image (./quickstart.sh image gpu, TORCH_VARIANT=cuda)

The same Dockerfile on x86_64 installs torch 2.14.1 (CUDA build) from PyPI with the NVIDIA CUDA runtime libraries it
depends on, flash-linear-attention 0.6.0 (strands-decider[cuda]) and Triton, plus the Debian packages gcc and
libc6-dev (Triton compiles a small launcher at run time). The NVIDIA libraries (nvidia-*, cuda-toolkit) are
proprietary NVIDIA software under the NVIDIA Software License Agreement and the CUDA Toolkit End User License
Agreement (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/). This sample doesn't include or redistribute them: your CodeBuild
project downloads them from PyPI when you build the GPU image, and you use them under NVIDIA's terms. The NVIDIA
driver on GPU nodes is installed and managed by Amazon EKS Auto Mode.

